--
--   Test Description
--
--   This test is intended to demonstrate the functionality when the transmit 
--   is disabled during normal operation and to check that the gem restarts
--   correctly.  Furthermore, this test is intended to test the GEMs 
--   ability to recover from error, provide access to the buffer descriptors 
--   and the transmit frames in a timely way.
--   
--
--   Functional Coverage
--   � Ensure proper operation of tx_go (tx enable bit).
--   � Ensure that when a disable tx bit is set tx does stop immediately
--   � Ensure writing to the base tx q ptr has no affect when tx_go is set.
--   � Ensure that when tx disable is set that pause frames halt immediately
--     for both software and hardware controlled pause frames
--   � Ensure that when transmit is re-enabled, operation is resumed from
--     an idle state, and not from anything left over.
--
--   Detailed Test Description
--
--   1. Initialise the GEM for 10M mode operation.
--   2. Enable transmit.
--   3. Transmit a 122 byte frame using DMA. During the frame keep writing 
--      a high to tx_go, then finally write tx_halt.
--      Check that the frame completes and that tx halts.
--   4. Transmit a frame using DMA. Disable transmit half way through the 
--      frame transmission. This should cause all TX mac and DMA operation to
--      stop immediately and dma reads. Check that it recovers the base 
--      queue pointer address.
--   5. Restart transmission and then try to write a new base queue pointer
--      whilst tx_go is active. This should have no affect and the frame 
--      should complete normally
--   6  Set full duplex to allow transmission of pause frames         
--   7. Insert a pause frame using the software control method.
--      During transmission disable transmit and check txd activity is 
--      immediately terminated.
--   8. Enable transmit and queue a DMA frame. Check that the DMA frame is
--      transmitted and not the pause frame.
--   9. Insert a pause frame using the hardware control method.
--      During transmission disable transmit and check txd activity is 
--      immediately terminated.
--  10. Enable transmit and queue a DMA frame. Check that the DMA frame is
--      transmitted and not the pause frame.
--  11. Finally transmit a good DMA frame and also a pause frame using the
--      software control method. Check that both are transmitted.
--  12. Check statistics to ensure that the above was handled correctly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

